# fake-hwclock
### The boards without a real time clock boot at the floor the kernel enforces: the release date
### of the kernel, raised to the time the image was made by the clock-epoch of the post-install
### of systemd. Loading the epoch saved at the last shutdown starts every boot from the closest
### known past, so the stamps of the journal stay near until timesyncd corrects the clock
PKG_VER=1.0
BUILD_PROCESS=none
PKG_TOOLCHAIN=gnu
